I was traveling this week, so the log and timestamps are a little unreliable,
I had to recreate the repo for this assignment and copy over the initial code
so the first few submissions copied from previous versions of this assignment
that I began. I made the first few commits as authentic as I could, commiting
the file creation first, then the first part, then the next, rather than one
big git push of everything I had done up to that point, in an attempt to show
the initial process.

I started this assignment by first writing the program defiition and initial
variable assignments.

I then implimented the code to open the source file and read the content, then
I wrote the code to prevent directories from being source files, and code
to reject source file not owned by root. I then wrote error checking code
and ran several tests.

I then wrote the code for the destination, checking if it exists, and if now,
making the destination file. Added a read and write loop to copy the contents
from source to destination
I then wrote code to close both files when the writing was done.

I then added error handling and checking and updated existing error checks,
then tested several different cases, including fake files, directories, 
empty files, and very large files and checked that the copied files were
correct.
